    "notes": "The AUTH_SIGNALS dictionary, lower-cased substring match: failed to authenticate, oauth session expired, session expired, not logged in, auth required, authentication failed, unauthorized. The last case is the point of the class and is deliberately `true`: the dictionary cannot tell a lost login from a review discussing one, so nothing protects that review except *where* Matches is called — only on a failure path, never over a reply that worked. See `an-ordinary-reply-mentioning-401-is-still-a-reply` in codex.vectors.json, which is the case that would break if that placement were ever widened."
